<urn:atm:triage:finding/RSH-014>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RSH-014" ;
  triage:title "Unix lifecycle thread exits on Ok(0) pipe-close without calling state_change.notify() — graceful-shutdown livelock on Unix (lifecycle_control.rs:217)" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/lifecycle_control.rs:217 — The Unix lifecycle thread's wake-pipe read loop exits silently on `Ok(0) => return` when the write end of the wake pipe is closed (e.g., during abnormal teardown or if install_platform_hooks panics after the thread is spawned). This return exits the thread without calling `state_change.notify()`. Any caller blocked in `wait_for_state_change` (e.g., the daemon main loop) is never woken, producing the same graceful-shutdown livelock on Unix that RSH-013 fixed for Windows. This is a pre-existing structural gap, not introduced by the RSH-013 fix, but exposed by the full-file scan of lifecycle_control.rs at 9e97934. Fix: replace `Ok(0) => return,` with `Ok(0) => { let _ = state_change.notify(); return; }`. Pair with a post-wakeup check of `terminate_requested()` in the main loop to distinguish a real signal from an EOF wake." ;
  triage:category "RSH" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-S" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-05-09T20:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/RSH-014/s4/1> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/feature-pS-s4-hardening/9e97934> .

